    "body": "pulse task #2716 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:211f259cb593d2aa195175fde74ae653 -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2716: Toggle loop-range content focus mode with Q\n\nOperation: 211f259cb593d2aa195175fde74ae653\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nUser request, 17 October 2026: add a toggleable Arrangement focus mode, provisionally bound to Q. The user creates a loop region to identify the timeline area of interest, then presses Q to show only tracks and clips with actual content inside that loop region, hiding other tracks/clips. Pressing Q again restores the normal view.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Use the canonical loop selection range as the focus interval; looping playback need not be toggled merely to focus.\n- Visibility reflects content intersecting the loop interval, including clips spanning a loop boundary, rather than requiring a clip to start inside it. Empty tracks and clips outside the interval are hidden in focus mode.\n- Focus is a reversible view filter; preserve project content, track/clip identities, selection, playback and saved musical edits. Leaving focus restores the normal track/clip view.\n- Updating the loop range while focus is on updates the visible content consistently. Handle absent/invalid ranges explicitly without deleting data or unintentionally hiding the whole project.\n- Q should respect text entry and existing shortcut contexts; inspect conflicts before assigning the provisional shortcut and report any conflict requiring a decision.\n- Verify mixed audio/MIDI, empty tracks, partial overlap and range boundaries, repeated toggling and changes to the loop interval, with targeted view/input tests and a finite optimized native checklist.\n\nPlanning capture only. Track resizing, clip resize edge panning, and loop-bar gesture changes are separate tickets; do not replace the running app while the user is testing.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
